%% PACT v1.0 — informative sequence for sections 11–12 and the approval example.
%% The gateway includes its requirement-publishing adapter in this example.
%% This illustrates a pending approval, not an absent or demonstrably invalid claim.
%% Approval routing, human roles, notification, and exception grants are external.
%% Fresh exchanges repeat all required checks; old terminal receipts stay immutable.
sequenceDiagram
    accTitle: PACT admission with external supervisor approval
    accDescr: A pending native approval produces a terminal DEFERRED result. If a supervisor later approves through the external system, the agent obtains a fresh requirement contract and submits a fresh presentation. Execution still requires current native authorization and execution checks.

    participant A as Agent
    participant G as Gateway
    participant V as PACT validator
    participant N as Native identity and policy
    participant H as External approval system

    A->>G: ContractRequest with intent and proposed operation
    G->>N: Authenticate and resolve native operation context
    N-->>G: Valid identity, key binding, and native context
    Note over G,N: Invalid authentication stops the exchange
    G-->>A: Signed RequirementContract C1 with one-use nonce
    A->>G: Signed Presentation P1 and actual request
    G->>V: Presentation and mapped native context
    V->>H: Resolve required approval reference
    H-->>V: Approval pending
    V-->>G: Signed DEFERRED receipt
    G-->>A: DEFERRED with bounded retry guidance and no execution

    Note over A,H: Exchange C1/P1 is terminal. The external workflow may continue after its expiry
    Note over H: Supervisor reviews under native policy

    opt External workflow later grants approval or a permitted exception
        H-->>A: Approval reference or trusted attestation
        Note over A,H: Notification and evidence retrieval are implementation-defined
        A->>G: Fresh ContractRequest for the intended operation
        G->>N: Refresh authentication and native operation context
        N-->>G: Current valid identity and context
        G-->>A: Fresh signed RequirementContract C2 with a new nonce
        A->>G: Fresh signed Presentation P2, approval reference, and actual request
        G->>V: Fresh presentation and mapped native context
        V->>H: Resolve authority, scope, validity, and current approval status
        H-->>V: Trusted approval evidence and status
        V->>V: Repeat all PACT checks against C2 and the actual request
        V-->>G: Signed admission receipt for P2

        alt ADMISSIBLE
            G->>N: Authorize exact operation with applicable approval or exception
            N-->>G: Current native authorization decision
            alt Native authorization allows and all execution conditions pass
                G->>G: Enforce once-only handoff, execute, and record attributable outcome
                G-->>A: Operation result
            else Native authorization or execution checks do not allow
                G-->>A: No execution with native reason
            end
        else INADMISSIBLE or DEFERRED
            G-->>A: Admission result with no execution
        end
    end

    Note over A,H: Pending, denied, expired, or revoked approval cannot authorize execution
